out 18 points is consistent with the polling, so the forecast stays near that level.", "watch": "A major scandal or a sharp national backlash environment could narrow the margin, though even a large shift would be unlikely to threaten the outcome.", "confidence": "medium", "notes": ["Incumbent Maura Healey (D) is running."]}, "overview": "Massachusetts governor is one of the safest Democratic-held seats on the 2026 map. Incumbent Maura Healey faces Republican Mike Minogue, who won his party's primary in early September, plus two minor independent candidates. The state's partisan lean favors Democrats by about 14 points, and Healey carries the added advantage of incumbency.\n\nPolling has been remarkably stable all year: recent surveys from UNH and UMass Amherst show Healey leading by 20 to 24 points, and the polling average sits near 22. All six major race raters call the contest Solid or Safe Democratic, and prediction markets price Healey's win odds at 95 to 96 percent. The campaign has centered on affordability, with both candidates proposing a gas tax holiday, but no evidence suggests the race is competitive.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-22", "p_dem": 0.9961, "margin": 18.83}, {"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.9968, "margin": 20.0}]}